In summary, using a thread-safe data structure can help ensure that the TCP connection event list and monitoring system are updated accurately and consistently across multiple threads, but it may also come with performance overhead. Therefore, it is important to carefully consider the trade-offs when deciding whether or not to use a thread-safe data structure in your application.']

