The function manages memory allocation and deallocation efficiently by using a cache of pre-allocated structures. If there are available entries in the cache, they are reused instead of allocating new memory. If there are no available entries in the cache or if the number of structures to be generated exceeds the size of the cache, new memory is allocated and the existing cache entries are deallocated.

The function also includes a mechanism for handling delays or failures in receiving necessary tag information from external sources by retrying failed requests and using cached values when possible.

