The `remove_rx_buffer` function removes the oldest node from the cache. It first checks if there are any nodes in the cache, and if not, it returns an error. The function then releases the lock on the cache and returns 0.

The `get_rx_buffer` function gets a node from the cache by removing it from the head of the linked list. If there are no available nodes in the cache, it returns NULL. The function then releases the lock on the cache and returns the retrieved node.

