The performance implications of this design are primarily focused on scalability and throughput under high-load conditions. To achieve this, the following optimizations can be made:

1. Use a lock-free data structure for the cache to reduce contention between threads. This can be achieved by using a hash table or a tree-based data structure instead of a linked list.
