5. Use a message passing interface between threads to reduce communication overhead between threads. This can be achieved by using a message queue or a shared memory region instead of direct function calls.
6. Implement a thread-safe mechanism for accessing the cache from multiple threads. This can be done by using locks, semaphores, or other synchronization primitives to ensure that only one thread accesses the cache at a time.

By implementing these optimizations, the performance of the RX buffer cache can be significantly improved under high-load conditions.']

