This code implements a linked list of NFAPI_CRC_INDICATION_PDU_T structures that can be dynamically grown and shrunk as needed. The linked list is protected by a semaphore, which ensures thread safety during read and write operations. The semaphore value is initialized from a runtime configuration file using standard library functions.

The code also includes a feature to monitor the list size and initiate garbage collection when the list exceeds a specified threshold. Garbage collection efficiently removes the least recently used elements from the list, without compromising data integrity.

To optimize performance, the function includes a logging mechanism with different verbosity levels (debug, info, warning, error) to track the number of elements added to the list and any errors during memory allocation or list operations. The logs are efficiently buffered using a circular buffer, which minimizes performance overhead during high-frequency events.

The function is designed to be resilient against external dependency failures, such as network latency, inconsistent data formats, and temporary outages. It includes retries with exponential backoff in case of transient failures, ensuring reliable operation under challenging conditions.

Overall, this code provides a robust and efficient solution for managing a dynamically growing linked list of NFAPI_CRC_INDICATION_PDU_T structures, using standard library functions and semaphores to ensure thread safety and data integrity.']

