To develop a C function to dynamically create and populate a linked list of `NFAPI_CRC_INDICATION_PDU_T` structures with randomized values, consider the following design:

1. Define a custom structure to hold the RX_UE_INFORMATION_TAG, RNTI, and CRC_INDICATION_REL8_TAG fields. This will serve as the basic unit of the linked list.
```c
typedef struct {
    uint32_t rx_ue_information_tag;
    uint16_t rnti;
    uint16_t crc_indication_rel8_tag;
} nfapi_crc_indication_pdu_t;
```
2. Define a linked list structure to hold the custom structures defined in step 1. This will be used to create and populate the linked list.
```c
typedef struct {
    struct nfapi_crc_indication_pdu_t *head;
} nfapi_crc_indication_list_t;
```
3. Define a function to dynamically allocate memory for a new `nfapi_crc_indication_pdu_t` structure and populate it with randomized values. This will be used to create new linked list nodes.
```c
void nfapi_create_crc_indication_pdu(struct nfapi_crc_indication_pdu_t **pdu) {
    *pdu = malloc(sizeof(**pdu));
    if (*pdu == NULL) {
        return;
    }

    (*pdu)->rx_ue_information_tag = rand();
    (*pdu)->rnti = rand();
    (*pdu)->crc_indication_rel8_tag = rand();
}
```
4. Define a function to dynamically allocate memory for a new `nfapi_crc_indication_list_t` structure and populate it with randomized values. This will be used to create the linked list.
```c
void nfapi_create_crc_indication_list(struct nfapi_crc_indication_list_t **list) {
    *list = malloc(sizeof(**list));
    if (*list == NULL) {
        return;
    }

    struct nfapi_crc_indication_pdu_t *node = NULL;
    while (nfapi_create_crc_indication_pdu(&node)) {
        struct nfapi_crc_indication_list_t *curr = *list;
        curr->head = node;
        curr = node;
        node = NULL;
    }
}
```
5. Define a function to free the memory allocated for a `nfapi_crc_indication_pdu_t` structure and any linked list nodes that are not referenced by other structures. This will be used to deallocate memory when it is no longer needed.
```c
void nfapi_free_crc_indication_pdu(struct nfapi_crc_indication_pdu_t *pdu) {
    if (pdu != NULL) {
        free(pdu);
    }
}
```
6. Define a function to free the memory allocated for a `nfapi_crc_indication_list_t` structure and any linked list nodes that are not referenced by other structures. This will be used to deallocate memory when it is no longer needed.
```c
void nfapi_free_crc_indication_list(struct nfapi_crc_indication_list_t *list) {
    if (list != NULL) {
        struct nfapi_crc_indication_pdu_t *node = list->head;
        while (node != NULL) {
            struct nfapi_crc_indication_pdu_t *next = node->next;
            nfapi_free_crc_indication_pdu(node);
            node = next;
        }
        free(list);
    }
}
