To ensure that cell identities do not conflict within the same bandwidth part, the function checks if any two cells have the same identity modulo their corresponding bandwidth parts. If a conflict is detected, the function increments the identity of the first cell until a conflict-free identity is found.

The function also manages memory allocation efficiently by adjusting the CRS power level for each cell based on its physical layer channel bandwidth. This ensures that the performance of the system remains optimal under varying network loads while minimizing fragmentation.

Finally, the function returns the initialized and populated dynamic array of `LTEPHYRACHConfig_t` structures.']

